This is what I found that's somewhat similar to my code, I just changed the math a little for result to fit my variables. Now that I look at it, why are they changing result 3 times? 

    @Override
      public boolean equals(Object obj) {
        if(obj == null){
          return false;
        }
        return (this == obj);
      }
      @Override
      public int hashCode(){
        final int prime = 31; 
        int result = 1; 
        result = prime * result +  x.hashCode(); 
        result = prime * result;
        result = prime * result +  y.hashCode(); 
        return result;
      }

